+# Answer: `fs.rmSync` options in Node 22
+
+## Short answer
+
+Use **`recursive: true`**:
+
+```js
+fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true });              // deletes the folder and everything in it
+fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }); // same, and no error if `dir` doesn't exist (like `rm -rf`)
+```
+
+## Options documented for `fs.rmSync(path[, options])` (Node 22)
+
+| Option       | Type      | Default | Meaning |
+|--------------|-----------|---------|---------|
+| `force`      | `boolean` | `false` | When `true`, exceptions are ignored if `path` does not exist. |
+| `maxRetries` | `integer` | `0`     | If an `EBUSY`, `EMFILE`, `ENFILE`, `ENOTEMPTY` or `EPERM` error happens, Node retries with a linear backoff that grows by `retryDelay` ms on each try. This is the number of retries. It is ignored unless `recursive` is `true`. |
+| `recursive`  | `boolean` | `false` | When `true`, does a recursive directory removal. In recursive mode, operations are retried on failure. |
+| `retryDelay` | `integer` | `100`   | How many milliseconds to wait between retries. It is ignored unless `recursive` is `true`. |
+
+Source: Node.js v22 docs, `fs.rmSync(path[, options])`: https://nodejs.org/docs/latest-v22.x/api/fs.html#fsrmsyncpath-options
+
+## Which one fixes it
+
+**`recursive: true`.** `force` does **not** fix it. `force` only stops the error when the path is missing. Without `recursive`, `rmSync` still refuses to delete a directory.
+
+One correction to the question: the error is not about the folder being non-empty. Without `recursive: true`, `fs.rmSync` throws on **any** directory, even an empty one. The error is `ERR_FS_EISDIR` ("Path is a directory"), not `ENOTEMPTY`.
+
+## Verified locally (Node v22.23.4)
+
+```
+fs.rmSync(nonEmptyDir)                      -> throws ERR_FS_EISDIR
+fs.rmSync(emptyDir)                         -> throws ERR_FS_EISDIR
+fs.rmSync(nonEmptyDir, {recursive: true})   -> removed (existsSync === false)
+fs.rmSync(missingPath)                      -> throws ENOENT
+fs.rmSync(missingPath, {force: true})       -> no error
+```
+
+The defaults come from Node's internal option validator (`node --expose-internals`, `internal/fs/utils.validateRmOptionsSync`):
+
+```
+{ recursive: false, force: false, retryDelay: 100, maxRetries: 0 }
+```
